{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 889,
    "dDurationMs": 5790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Winter is unquestionably the best season - for\nskiing. And for full moons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6679,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're lucky enough to have winters because\nthe earth's plane of rotation is tilted relative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11269,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to its orbit. This means that when part of\nthe earth is tilted towards the sun, the sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15409,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stays in the sky for a longer amount of time\neach day, and it's warm out. Summer! Of course,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21209,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when that part of the earth is tilted away\nfrom the sun, the sun is lower in the sky"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24619,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and doesn't stay up as long. This might make\nwinter darker, but you can think of it as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28519,
    "dDurationMs": 5710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bonus time pointing towards interstellar space!\nAnd, as I said before, winter has the best"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34229,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "full moons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35369,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The moon is new when it's on the same side\nof the earth as the sun, and it doesn't reflect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39369,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any light on us. This also means the new moon\ngenerally mirrors the sun on its journey across"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44319,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sky - it more or less rises and sets with\nthe sun and follows a similar path. On the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49839,
    "dDurationMs": 4019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other hand, the moon is full when it's on\nthe opposite side of the earth from the sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53858,
    "dDurationMs": 3261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its whole face reflecting the sun's light\nback at us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57119,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because of this opposite position, a full\nmoon is only ever up at night, rising at sunset"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62259,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and setting at sunrise, and it consequently\nalso behaves the way the sun does in the opposite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67099,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "season. When a part of the earth is tilted\ntowards the full moon, it's tilted away from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71909,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sun - and vice versa. So a summer full\nmoon is like a winter sun - only appearing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77299,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a few hours and staying close to the horizon.\nBut a winter full moon is like a summer sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82659,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- it's up for a long time and takes a high\npath through the sky. In the darkest months,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87859,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the moon, at least when it's full, gives us\nlong, beautifully lit nights. Combined with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92959,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a quiet blanket of snow and the shimmering\naurora, how can you not love winter?"
    } ]
  } ]
}
